 "decisions": "CRITICAL (data-part-critical): (1) studio-tgb-carry, the carry-over question (switching between builder and text view, or editing a key/option/type, raises \"carry the rename over?\"): answering \"carry\" rewrites other values and references, \"keep\" drops the old values, and the \"carried\" state holds the only way back (Undo). Both states, ask and done, are one part with data-state; every explanation, list, warning, reference button and choice inside is a protected child studio-tgb-carry-*. (2) studio-tgb-alert, the \"group never closed\" alert (role=alert, a warning, with a button that edits the text): hard errors change what the chat reads, so a pack may give it tokens only. Both appear in the list builder (#tgBanners, also inside the row-editor sheet for the carry) and in the combined view.\nAlready critical by the shell and reused unchanged: studio-undo-toast (a toast with an action) carries the way back of: delete a row, change type that drops options, close a group, carry over, update references. The shell passes critical only through A.openSheet({critical:true}); no sheet of the builder is critical (see below).\nLEFT NON-CRITICAL: studio-tgb-banner (info notes: group split, swallowed, source off, \"left as is\"): informational, offer no choice, change nothing. The add sheet and the paste sheet (add rows, nothing is dropped). The row-editor sheet (tgside): it carries a Delete button (danger), but Delete is immediate with a critical Undo toast, and the carry question inside it is its own critical part; marking the whole editor sheet critical would force every field to be named studio-critical-*. Editor Delete, option delete, duplicate: immediate, undoable through the header Undo and (for rows) the Undo toast. The row menu (\"Delete\" item, class danger) comes from A.openMenu in slice1.js and I could not make it critical without editing that file (see the report question). Combined-view and preview parts: nothing there writes or drops author data (the preview sandbox values are synthetic).\nNOT SAFE (ancestors, or can hold a critical element in some state): studio-tgb (page body), studio-tgb-banners (holds the carry and the alert), studio-tgb-cols and studio-tgb-editor and studio-tgb-page (in an edge case, resizing while the editor sheet is open, #tgEd of the page or inline editor receives the carry question because inSheet() is still true), studio-tgb-merged and studio-tgb-merged-section (hold the alert), and every protected child. SAFE: everything else; none of them is ever a critical element, inside one, or an ancestor of one (checked with the census in the states listed in the report; the resize edge case is a code-reading argument, not a runtime check)."
}